# SRG-APP-000805-WSR-000140  -  CAT II
# The web server must automatically generate audit records of the
# enforcement actions.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000805-WSR-000140
group:           V-264341
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003938
control_rev5:    CM-5

contribution:    Splunk writes a record of every change made to its own configuration
                 files, including the values that changed, and queues its audit trail to an
                 index; it also holds the capability that permits audit settings to be
                 altered, so the record cannot be quietly narrowed by an ordinary user.

governs:         audit.conf - The audit trail Splunk keeps of its own activity, and how those records
                 are signed.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] disabled in false|0
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] mode in auto|diff
check:           audit.conf [auditTrail] queueing in true|1
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] denylist absent
check:           server.conf [config_change_tracker] exclude_fields absent

external:        Enforcement actions by components in front of the web interface - a
                 reverse proxy's denials, for example - carried by that component.
external:        Operating system level access denials against the installation's files,
                 carried by the operating system's own audit subsystem.
external:        Which roles hold the change_audit capability that permits audit settings
                 to be altered is assessed under the role requirement,
                 SRG-APP-000380-WSR-000072 (authorize.conf.spec:483).

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000805-WSR-000140 check and fix text;
                 server.conf.spec:599 (disabled, default false), server.conf.spec:608
                 (mode, default auto), server.conf.spec:636 (denylist),
                 server.conf.spec:661 (exclude_fields), audit.conf.spec:24 (queueing,
                 default true), authorize.conf.spec:483 ([capability::change_audit])
finding:         Configuration change tracking is switched off, set to track-only, or
                 narrowed by a denylist or excluded fields, or the audit trail is not
                 queued to an index, so the web server does not automatically generate
                 records of the enforcement actions it takes.
